1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,400
WHAT IF HYDROGEN VANISHED?

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:08,330
1 — Atomic number
The simplest atom: one proton, one electron.

3
00:00:08,330 --> 00:00:13,290
IMPOSSIBLE — A thought experiment
Matter can't just disappear. But the numbers tell a story.

4
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:18,800
74% — Of ordinary matter, by mass
Hydrogen. Helium is about 24%. Everything else: about 2%.

5
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:24,040
92% — Of all atoms
More than 9 in 10 atoms in the universe are hydrogen.

6
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:28,370
73.8% — Of the sun's surface, by mass
The Sun is mostly hydrogen fuel.

7
00:00:28,370 --> 00:00:34,130
~62% — Of the atoms in your body
Only about 10% of your mass, but most of your atoms.

8
00:00:34,630 --> 00:00:37,230
NOW DELETE IT.

9
00:00:37,230 --> 00:00:40,530
T = 0
Every hydrogen atom. Everywhere. At once.

10
00:00:41,030 --> 00:00:45,870
−62% — Of your atoms, instantly
About 7 kg of a 70 kg person, gone.

11
00:00:45,870 --> 00:00:51,460
~60% — Of your body is water
Water is 2 hydrogens + 1 oxygen. Only the oxygen would remain.

12
00:00:51,460 --> 00:00:57,220
3.1 billion — Dna base pairs per genome copy
Each pair is held together by 2 or 3 hydrogen bonds.

13
00:00:57,220 --> 00:01:01,320
0 — Living cells left
Every protein, membrane and gene contains hydrogen.

14
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:05,350
1.4 × 10²¹ kg — Of ocean water
About 1.34 billion cubic kilometres.

15
00:01:05,350 --> 00:01:10,480
1.24 × 10²¹ kg — Of oxygen left behind
Hydrogen is 11.2% of water's mass. The other 88.8% stays.

16
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:15,490
≈240× — The mass of today's atmosphere
If that oxygen became a gas layer around Earth...

17
00:01:15,490 --> 00:01:20,790
~240 atm — At the surface · venus: 92
...it would press about 240 times harder than today's air.

18
00:01:21,290 --> 00:01:25,100
≈80% — Of humanity's energy
comes from coal, oil and gas.

19
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:31,030
CH₄ → C — Methane loses 4 of its 5 atoms
Oil and gas are hydrocarbons. Without hydrogen, only carbon is left.

20
00:01:31,530 --> 00:01:35,400
600 million t — Of hydrogen fused every second
This is what powers sunlight.

21
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:41,560
~27–30% — Of the sun's mass remains
Fusion stops. Mostly helium is left, with under a third of the gravity.

22
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:47,530
8 min 19 s — Light travel time, sun to earth
Changes in gravity travel at the speed of light too.

23
00:01:47,530 --> 00:01:53,120
29.8 km/s — Earth's speed around the sun
To escape the Sun from here, you need 42.1 km/s.

24
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:59,390
22–23 km/s — The new escape speed
With under a third of the Sun's mass left, Earth is suddenly too fast.

25
00:01:59,390 --> 00:02:03,550
EARTH LEAVES ITS ORBIT.
About 8 minutes after the change.

26
00:02:04,050 --> 00:02:09,290
318 — Earth masses: jupiter
About three-quarters hydrogen, like most stars. Most of it would vanish.

27
00:02:09,290 --> 00:02:14,590
4.9% — Ordinary matter in the universe
Dark energy (~68.5%) and dark matter (~26.5%) would be untouched.

28
00:02:14,590 --> 00:02:20,180
≈3.6% — Of the universe is hydrogen
The universe would barely lose weight. It would lose its light.

29
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:25,810
13.8 billion yrs — Age of the universe
Hydrogen atoms formed about 380,000 years after the Big Bang.

30
00:02:25,810 --> 00:02:30,010
EVERYTHING YOU KNOW IS BUILT ON ATOM NUMBER 1.

31
00:02:30,010 --> 00:02:36,010
WHICH ELEMENT WOULD YOU REMOVE NEXT?

